{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Persistent low bias: model forecasts are systematically below realized prices across the full 30-day horizon (often by ~2–5 EUR, sometimes more). Apply an upward level shift to the entire path.",
    "Trend/lag error in rising regimes: when the recent history transitions from a drawdown to an upswing, the model underreacts and lags the rally by several days. Add positive momentum (steepen the slope) when the last 5–10 days show higher highs/higher lows.",
    "Horizon-dependent bias: the underprediction grows with forecast horizon (errors tend to widen after ~day 7–10). Use a horizon-increasing uplift (e.g., small +EUR/day ramp) rather than a flat adjustment only.",
    "Over-mean-reversion: forecasts revert back toward ~63–66 even when the market breaks out to ~68–70. Reduce mean-reversion strength when price is making a regime shift (e.g., breaks above recent 20–30d range).",
    "Ceiling/volatility compression: model caps peaks and smooths volatility; true outcomes show larger, sustained upward moves. Inflate forecast volatility/upper tail during bullish breakouts (allow higher highs instead of clipping)."
  ]
}
